course: dictionary
lesson: 11024
title: Wavy
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Wavy is an adjective. It describes something that has curves like waves, so it is not straight. You can say «wavy hair» or «a wavy line». Picture the sea rolling in: each curve goes up and then down again.
explain: Look at the words around wavy to check its meaning. «Oak leaves have wavy edges and acorns sit in little cups.» Leaves do not have straight edges with wavy ones being straight, so the edges must curve up and down. Try the swap test: put "curvy like waves" in place of wavy, and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Scientists and artists use wavy lines too. In science, sound and light are often drawn as wavy lines on diagrams, to show how they move up and down. In art and maths, you can draw a wavy line on paper, and you will know straight from wavy by looking at it.
fact: Wavy means having curves like waves, not straight.
fact: «Oak leaves have wavy edges» means the edges of the leaves curve in and out.
fact: «The Giraffe grew... little wavy grey lines on their backs» describes lines that curve up and down, not straight stripes.
fact: In science, sound and light are often shown as wavy lines on diagrams.
fact: Wavy is an adjective, and its other forms are wavier and waviest.
exercise: «Oak leaves have wavy edges and acorns sit in little cups.» What does wavy mean here? | Shiny and green | Sharp, like a knife | Straight and smooth | *Curved up and down, like waves
exercise: Which line is wavy? | A line that goes dead straight across the page | *A line that curves up and down like waves | A single dot | A ruler's straight edge
exercise: «Newts... in spring the male great crested newt grows a tall wavy crest.» Find and copy the word that describes the shape of the crest. | newt | *wavy | crest | tall
test: Ella says her hair is wavy. What does she mean? | Her hair is very short | Her hair is as straight as a ruler | Her hair is wet from the bath | *Her hair has gentle curves, like waves
test: A science book draws sound as wavy lines. What do the wavy lines show? | Sleepy animals | Hard facts to learn | A straight road | *The way sound goes up and down
exam: «Oak leaves have wavy edges.» Which word means the opposite of wavy? | *Straight | Round | Bumpy | Curly
